In this research, we are focused on novel feature selection methods. Principal component analysis (PCA) is a well-explored feature reduction method that uses an orthogonal transformation to convert a set of observations of possibly correlated variables into a set of values of linearly uncorrelated variables called principal components. Oliveira has illustrated the use of PCA on spam database (Oliveira 2019). Park and Klabjan (2018) also explored conventional and variants PCA on spam dataset. We have added a short discussion in Sect. 3.5. Our goal was to optimize the classiﬁcation results using feature selection methods, and the proposed ‘‘Greedy Selection Strategy’’ can carry out the training process in a faster way and yields better result.
These selected/trained features are then converted into an understandable form for algorithms. Finally, an algorithm runs over the classiﬁers during classiﬁcation stage.

